<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Modena and Reggio</h1><p class="st-meta">1452 CE – 1859 CE · capital Modena</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Este duchy that became the family's main state after the loss of Ferrara, lasting until Italian unification in 1859.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1452 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Frederick III</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borso-deste">Borso d'Este</a> duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia">Reggio</a>, imperial fiefs held alongside the papal <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-ferrara">Duchy of Ferrara</a>. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> in 1598, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-d-este-duke-of-modena">Cesare d'Este</a> moved his court to Modena, which became the capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-este">Este</a> rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> as a capital, with a ducal palace and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biblioteca-estense">Biblioteca Estense</a>, where the scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-antonio-muratori">Ludovico Antonio Muratori</a> worked as librarian. The duchy added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirandola">Mirandola</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-correggio">Correggio</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-novellara">Novellara</a>. After French occupation from 1796, when it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cispadane-republic">Cispadane Republic</a>, the restored duchy passed in 1814 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-iv-duke-of-modena">Francis IV of Austria-Este</a>, who ruled harshly and executed the revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciro-menotti">Ciro Menotti</a> in 1831.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Francis V fled after the Austrian defeat in 1859. The duchy joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-provinces-of-central-italy">United Provinces of Central Italy</a> and was annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a> in 1860.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-modena-and-reggio.jpg" alt="Duchy of Modena and Reggio" width="320" height="235"><figcaption>Image: Durero · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ducado_de_Modena_(antes_de_1830).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1452 CE – 1859 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Modena</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Borso d'Este, Cesare d'Este, Francis IV of Modena</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Emilian, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Modena, Este Modena</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1656&amp;focus=duchy-of-modena-and-reggio" aria-label="Duchy of Modena and Reggio on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4941 599 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Modena and Reggio lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5261 855L5243 874M5261 855L5277 849M5261 855L5229 694M5261 855L5271 860M5261 855L5381 747M5261 855L5261 855M5261 855L5264 848M5261 855L5270 844M5261 855L5256 849M5261 855L5271 1103"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5243 874h0M5277 849h0M5229 694h0M5271 860h0M5381 747h0M5261 855h0M5264 848h0M5270 844h0M5256 849h0M5271 1103h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5261 855h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5261 855h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Modena. <a href="/atlas?year=1656&amp;focus=duchy-of-modena-and-reggio">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
